Now it is lunch time.
I step outside from the office.
It is very sunny outside.
It is very hot on the street.
I go to a nearby juice shop.
I ask the shopkeeper for a lime juice.
"I want a cold lime juice," I say.
"Do you want sugar or salt?" he asks.
"Sugar is enough," I reply.
He gives me the lime juice.
I drink it.
It is very cold.
In this heat, this is very good.
It is twenty rupees.
I give twenty rupees.
I walk back to the office.
